# CHARACTERS

JUDGE HORNBILL, an elderly hornbill who enjoys procedure almost as much as fruit.

AGRA, matriarch of a leafcutter-ant colony and guardian of its fungus gardens.

NINO, a flamboyant weaver bird and obsessive nest-builder.

SPINNER, an orb-weaver spider, dry, exact, and perpetually repairing something.

PROFESSOR FINN, a cichlid who treats every puddle like a university department.

SKYSHOT, an arowana with excellent aim and a slightly inflated opinion of it.

DAME DAMSEL, a beaver engineer who thinks in gradients, leaks, and timber.

BURR, a burrowing rodent who considers tunnels the highest form of civilization.

MARA, a mycorrhizal fungus speaking through mushrooms and roots.

TIK, a termite architect.

PIP, a tree frog.

RIVER, the voice of moving water.

BAOBAB, an old tree.

PARROT, unofficial journalist of the jungle.

ENSEMBLE, insects, fish, birds, mammals, fungi, plants, and whoever else can fit onstage.

# ACT ONE - PRIVATE GENIUS

## SCENE 1 - THE COURT OF ORIGINAL IDEAS

EXT. GREAT CLEARING - MORNING

A gigantic tree rises at center stage. Roots make natural benches.
A stream curls around one side of the playing space.

PARROT hops onto a branch carrying a rolled leaf.

PARROT
Breaking news! Emergency! Scandal!
Possibly snacks!

JUDGE HORNBILL
Parrot.

PARROT
Yes, Your Beakship?

JUDGE HORNBILL
Just read the notice.

PARROT
Right.

(reading)

"All residents are summoned to determine
who owns the jungle's ideas."

The clearing erupts.

NINO
Finally.

SPINNER
This will end badly.

BURR
Can I own silence?

PARROT
You'd have to demonstrate prior use.

BURR
I've been underground for six years.

JUDGE HORNBILL bangs a seedpod.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Order. We have received seventeen
complaints, nine counterclaims, three
threats involving stinging, and one
application to copyright the sunrise.

BAOBAB
That was Parrot.

PARROT
I withdrew it.

AGRA marches in with a column of ants carrying leaf fragments.

AGRA
My colony files first.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Claim?

AGRA
Fungus farming.

MARA
Excuse me?

AGRA
Not fungus. Fungus farming.

She indicates the ants.

AGRA (CONT'D)
We cut leaves, clean them, carry them
underground, prepare the substrate and
grow the fungus that feeds our colony.

PARROT
So you invented agriculture?

AGRA
We didn't say that.

PARROT
You strongly implied it.

AGRA
We invented our agriculture.

NINO swoops down carrying a grass strand.

NINO
Fine. Then I claim weaving.

He ties a dazzling knot.

NINO (CONT'D)
Observe.

Everyone leans closer.

NINO immediately covers the knot with his wing.

NINO (CONT'D)
Not that closely.

SPINNER descends on silk.

SPINNER
If we're doing this, I claim tensioned
fiber architecture.

NINO
That's weaving.

SPINNER
It's a web.

NINO
String arranged in space.

SPINNER
Your nest is a bag with ambition.

NINO
Take that back.

SPINNER
No.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Excellent. We're six minutes in and
already insulting architecture.

A SPLASH.

SKYSHOT rises from the stream.

SKYSHOT
I claim ballistic entomology.

PIP
You mean jumping at bugs?

SKYSHOT
I mean launching from water with enough
precision to grab prey above the surface.

PIP
So, jumping at bugs.

SKYSHOT
With geometry.

PROFESSOR FINN surfaces.

PROFESSOR FINN
I claim aquatic parental innovation.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Meaning?

PROFESSOR FINN
Nest defense, brood care, mouthbrooding,
depending on the cichlid. We have range.

PARROT
Can you copyright parenting?

PROFESSOR FINN
Parents have tried.

DAME DAMSEL enters dragging a branch twice her size.

DAME DAMSEL
Move.

Everyone moves.

She drops it.

DAME DAMSEL (CONT'D)
Water engineering.

RIVER
I object already.

DAME DAMSEL
Dams slow flow, create ponds, change
habitat, hold sediment--

RIVER
Yes. I noticed.

BURR pops from a hole.

BURR
Tunnel engineering.

TIK, the termite, appears beside him.

TIK
Excuse me?

BURR
Here we go.

TIK
Ventilation. Temperature regulation.
Load-bearing chambers. We've been doing
subterranean architecture forever.

BURR
Your walls taste terrible.

TIK
They're not lunch.

BURR
Everything underground is potentially
lunch.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Enough.

He surveys them.

JUDGE HORNBILL (CONT'D)
Each claimant will explain what makes
their knowledge theirs.

AGRA
Easy. We learned it.

NINO
We perfected it.

SPINNER
We embody it.

DAME DAMSEL
We work for it.

SKYSHOT
We're awesome at it.

PROFESSOR FINN
Ignore him.

JUDGE HORNBILL
And what happens when another creature
copies you?

A beat.

NINO
They owe me.

AGRA
They stop.

SPINNER
Depends whether the copying is competent.

BURR
I hide deeper.

DAME DAMSEL
I send an invoice.

RIVER
To whom?

DAME DAMSEL
Still designing that part.

MARA
Interesting.

Everyone turns toward a cluster of mushrooms.

MARA (CONT'D)
You all speak as though knowledge grew
inside sealed jars.

AGRA
Our fungus grows inside chambers.

MARA
Not the same thing.

MARA's underground threads glow faintly across the stage.

MARA (CONT'D)
But continue.

I enjoy watching animals discover
philosophy.

BLACKOUT.

## SCENE 2 - THE LICENSE BOOM

EXT. JUNGLE - LATER

A comic montage.

PARROT hangs signs.

PARROT
"PRIVATE TECHNIQUE."

Another.

PARROT (CONT'D)
"NO OBSERVATION WITHOUT PERMISSION."

Another.

PARROT (CONT'D)
"LOOKING AT THIS NEST CONSTITUTES
ACCEPTANCE OF TERMS."

NINO
Higher.

PARROT
Nobody can read it higher.

NINO
Exactly.

At the ant colony, AGRA guards an entrance.

A YOUNG ANT approaches.

YOUNG ANT
Queen Agra, the neighboring colony lost
their garden in a flood. They asked for
a little starter fungus.

AGRA
No.

YOUNG ANT
They're hungry.

AGRA
If we share cultures, everyone will farm
our strain.

MARA
Your strain?

AGRA
Please don't start.

MARA
I haven't started. I've been growing for
millions of years.

Across the stage, SPINNER catches PIP staring.

SPINNER
Are you measuring my radial threads?

PIP
I'm sitting here.

SPINNER
Suspiciously.

PIP
I am a frog.

SPINNER
Exactly what an industrial spy would say.

At the stream, SKYSHOT addresses three young fish.

SKYSHOT
Rule one of aerial hunting--

He notices PROFESSOR FINN.

SKYSHOT (CONT'D)
Private lesson.

PROFESSOR FINN
I wasn't listening.

SKYSHOT
Your ear is facing me.

PROFESSOR FINN
Fish don't have external ears.

SKYSHOT
See? Always stealing knowledge.

DAME DAMSEL puts a toll gate across a tiny side channel.

RIVER
What is that?

DAME DAMSEL
Infrastructure access fee.

RIVER
I'm water.

DAME DAMSEL
And now you're premium water.

The ensemble laughs.

Then the laughter thins.

A group of birds tries to repair a storm-damaged nest.

NINO sees them struggling.

YOUNG BIRD
Nino, how do you anchor the first loop?

NINO
Trade secret.

YOUNG BIRD
One loop.

NINO
That's how it begins.

He flies away.

SPINNER watches.

SPINNER
You could've shown them.

NINO
You could publish your web pattern.

SPINNER
That's different.

NINO
Naturally.

They separate.

BAOBAB rustles.

BAOBAB
Funny.

PARROT
What's funny?

BAOBAB
Everyone wants recognition for being
original.

PARROT
And?

BAOBAB
Nobody remembers who invented shade.

## SCENE 3 - DEMONSTRATION DAY

EXT. GREAT CLEARING - AFTERNOON

JUDGE HORNBILL has ordered demonstrations.

JUDGE HORNBILL
If we're going to protect knowledge, we
should understand what we're protecting.

NINO steps forward.

NINO
At last, culture.

He loops grass around a flexible branch.

NINO (CONT'D)
A good nest isn't just a pile.

You choose fibers that bend without
snapping. You anchor. Loop. Pull.
Interlock.

PIP
You just taught us.

NINO freezes.

NINO
Forget that.

PIP
Already practicing.

NINO
Frog!

PIP
Bird!

SPINNER takes center.

She releases silk.

SPINNER
A web responds to wind, prey, available
supports, damage, humidity--

NINO
And fashion?

SPINNER
No.

NINO
Sad.

SPINNER
Some threads frame the structure. Others
capture prey. I rebuild when conditions
change.

JUDGE HORNBILL
So the design isn't fixed?

SPINNER
Of course not. The environment edits it.

MARA
Interesting phrase.

SPINNER
Don't.

BURR demonstrates a tunnel with sticks.

BURR
If soil is loose, you brace. If it's wet,
you change direction. If roots are here,
you work around them.

BAOBAB
Thank you.

BURR
Mostly.

TIK
Termite mounds also exploit airflow and
thermal gradients.

BURR
Show-off.

TIK
You eat roots.

BURR
We all have hobbies.

DAME DAMSEL builds a miniature dam.

DAME DAMSEL
Water pushes. Wood resists. Mud seals.
But the important part is reading the
current.

RIVER
Finally somebody asks what I'm doing.

DAME DAMSEL
I didn't say ask.

RIVER
Close enough.

SKYSHOT circles below an overhanging branch.

A toy insect is perched above.

SKYSHOT
Watch.

He bursts upward and knocks it down.

CHEERS.

SKYSHOT lands with maximum dignity.

SKYSHOT (CONT'D)
Natural talent.

PROFESSOR FINN
And water refraction, body mechanics,
practice, prey behavior--

SKYSHOT
Natural. Talent.

PROFESSOR FINN
Fine.

AGRA's workers bring leaves toward a model fungus garden.

AGRA
We don't eat most of these leaves
directly. We process plant material and
cultivate our food.

MARA
And the fungus breaks down material the
ants can't efficiently use alone.

AGRA
Yes.

MARA
So your famous secret is already a
partnership.

Silence.

AGRA
Objection.

JUDGE HORNBILL
To biology?

AGRA
To her tone.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Overruled.

MARA
You tend fungus. Fungus feeds ants.
Plants feed fungus. Soil supports plants.
Microbes recycle what dies.

She looks around.

MARA (CONT'D)
Where exactly would you draw the fence?

AGRA
Around my colony.

MARA
Roots cross it.

AGRA
Then underground.

MARA
My threads cross that.

AGRA
You're difficult.

MARA
I'm a fungus. Boundaries are suggestions.

The ensemble laughs.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Court adjourned until tomorrow.

He raises the seedpod.

JUDGE HORNBILL (CONT'D)
Nobody invent anything overnight.

PARROT
What if inspiration strikes?

JUDGE HORNBILL
Write it on a leaf.

PARROT
And register it?

JUDGE HORNBILL
Go home.

BLACKOUT.

# ACT TWO - THE PRICE OF SECRETS

## SCENE 4 - THE RAIN

EXT. JUNGLE - NIGHT

Thunder.

Rain begins gently, then becomes violent.

RIVER
Coming through.

DAME DAMSEL
That's a lot of water.

RIVER
Premium water.

DAME DAMSEL
Not now.

She races toward her dam.

BURR emerges, soaked.

BURR
My eastern tunnel's flooding!

DAME DAMSEL
Dig an overflow channel.

BURR
Where?

DAME DAMSEL
Down-gradient.

BURR
Which way is down-gradient underground?

TIK
I can help.

BURR
Your ventilation design is proprietary.

TIK
You mocked it.

BURR
I was younger then.

TIK
That was this morning.

A tree limb crashes.

NINO's nest swings wildly.

YOUNG BIRD
The anchor!

NINO
Double-loop it!

YOUNG BIRD
How?

NINO hesitates.

Another gust.

NINO
Like this!

He demonstrates rapidly.

NINO (CONT'D)
Under, around, back through! Pull!

The young bird copies him.

The nest holds.

NINO stares at it.

YOUNG BIRD
Thanks.

NINO
Yeah.

Don't tell anyone.

YOUNG BIRD
Everyone just saw.

NINO looks at the audience.

NINO
Terrific.

Elsewhere, AGRA's colony floods.

YOUNG ANT
The fungus chamber!

AGRA
Move the brood!

MARA
Higher ground. There's a dry root cavity
beneath Baobab.

AGRA
How do you know?

MARA
I'm connected to it.

AGRA
Can we use it?

MARA
Of course.

AGRA
No license?

MARA
Agra, you're drowning.

AGRA
Right.

They rush.

At the stream, a small pool is cut off by debris.

PROFESSOR FINN
Fry trapped!

SKYSHOT
I'll clear it.

PROFESSOR FINN
You can't jump through a log.

SKYSHOT
Watch me.

He tries.

THUD.

SKYSHOT (CONT'D)
I have revised my position.

DAME DAMSEL
I can redirect the side flow.

BURR
I can tunnel under the debris.

TIK
I can tell you where the bank will hold.

SPINNER
I can mark the safest line between roots.

PROFESSOR FINN
Do it.

Everyone works.

The water shifts.

The trapped fish escape.

A pause.

They stare at one another.

BURR
Did we just collaborate?

DAME DAMSEL
Temporary emergency exception.

SPINNER
Obviously.

MARA
Obviously.

LIGHTS FADE.

## SCENE 5 - AFTER THE STORM

EXT. GREAT CLEARING - MORNING

Broken branches. Mud. Torn leaves.

The jungle looks bruised.

PARROT
Damage report.

(reading)

Three nests lost. Two tunnels collapsed.
One dam partially breached. Ant fungus
garden damaged. Several webs gone.

SPINNER
All my webs are gone.

PARROT
Right. Several sounds kinder.

SPINNER
Don't make my tragedy editorial.

NINO examines a ruined nest.

NINO
I spent eleven days on that.

SPINNER
I spent a night on mine.

NINO
Exactly.

SPINNER
That wasn't agreement.

AGRA enters.

AGRA
We lost half the garden.

MARA
The surviving culture can regrow.

AGRA
Slowly.

A YOUNG ANT whispers to her.

YOUNG ANT
The neighboring colony offered us some
of theirs.

AGRA
The colony we refused?

YOUNG ANT
Yes.

AGRA
Why?

YOUNG ANT
They said fungus doesn't care about
pride.

MARA
Smart fungus.

AGRA
You are enjoying this.

MARA
A little.

JUDGE HORNBILL enters.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Court resumes.

NINO
Seriously?

JUDGE HORNBILL
Especially seriously.

They gather.

JUDGE HORNBILL (CONT'D)
Last night, how many of you used knowledge
belonging to another species?

No one raises anything.

JUDGE HORNBILL (CONT'D)
Fine.

How many would have lost offspring,
homes, food, or neighbors without it?

Slowly, almost everyone raises a limb,
wing, fin, antenna, or leaf.

JUDGE HORNBILL (CONT'D)
Interesting.

SKYSHOT
Emergency conditions.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Does water know it's an emergency?

RIVER
I barely know it's Tuesday.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Does a falling branch pause to check
licensing terms?

BAOBAB
Never has.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Then perhaps the problem isn't whether
knowledge has value.

Perhaps the problem is believing value
only exists when knowledge is withheld.

AGRA
That's too simple.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Good.

Then complicate it.

## SCENE 6 - THE ARGUMENT

EXT. CLEARING - CONTINUOUS

AGRA steps forward.

AGRA
Sharing isn't automatically noble.

My workers spend their lives maintaining
our garden.

If another colony takes everything we've
learned and gives nothing back, that's
not cooperation.

NINO
Exactly.

I practice. I fail. I rebuild.

If someone copies the result and calls
themselves the genius, I'm allowed to be
annoyed.

SPINNER
Very annoyed.

PROFESSOR FINN
Recognition matters.

DAME DAMSEL
So does responsibility.

If I teach someone to alter a stream and
they flood three burrows, "knowledge
should be free" won't dry anybody's bed.

BURR
Thank you.

MARA
Good.

Everyone turns.

MARA (CONT'D)
Now we're finally talking about the real
thing.

Not ownership.

Relationships.

TIK
Explain.

MARA
A forest isn't generous because nobody
has boundaries.

It survives because boundaries are
porous enough for exchange.

Roots take water.

Leaves give sugars.

Fungi trade minerals.

Pollinators move pollen.

Predators move energy.

Decomposers return bodies to soil.

Nothing gives everything.

Nothing keeps everything.

PIP
So what's the rule?

MARA
There isn't one.

PARROT
Terrible slogan.

MARA
Life isn't a slogan.

PARROT
Worse.

NINO
Then what are we supposed to do?

BAOBAB speaks.

BAOBAB
Pay attention.

Everyone quiets.

BAOBAB (CONT'D)
A forest is an argument that has lasted
long enough to become music.

PARROT
That's annoyingly good.

BAOBAB
Thank you.

BAOBAB's branches move.

BAOBAB (CONT'D)
You want credit? Give credit.

You want respect? Ask permission when
permission matters.

You want survival?

Share what must be shared.

And when you borrow from the living world,
remember that you are borrowing from
relatives.

AGRA
Relatives?

BAOBAB
Very distant relatives.

BURR
How distant?

BAOBAB
Please don't make me explain evolution
before lunch.

## SCENE 7 - THE SECOND CRISIS

EXT. RIVERBANK - DAYS LATER

Heat.

The stream is shrinking.

RIVER
I'm low.

DAME DAMSEL
I can see that.

RIVER
Just checking.

DAME DAMSEL studies the bank.

DAME DAMSEL
If I reinforce here, I can hold a deeper
pool.

PROFESSOR FINN
That could keep fish alive.

PIP
And frogs.

SKYSHOT
And my lunch.

PIP
Less inspiring.

DAME DAMSEL
But slowing water here could reduce flow
downstream.

BURR
My burrow is downstream.

AGRA
So is one of our foraging routes.

NINO
And my favorite bathing branch.

SPINNER
Tragic.

NINO
Thank you.

SPINNER
Still not agreement.

DAME DAMSEL
We need information.

BURR
My tunnels show where the soil stays damp.

TIK
Our mound temperatures indicate where
air and moisture move.

BAOBAB
My roots know where the deeper water is.

MARA
And I connect roots across much of this
bank.

PROFESSOR FINN
Fish can tell you which pools remain
oxygenated.

SKYSHOT
I can tell you where insects gather.

PIP
I can tell you where mosquitoes gather.

SKYSHOT
Same department.

DAME DAMSEL
All right.

Everyone talks.

DAME DAMSEL draws a map in mud.

SPINNER lays silk lines across it.

BURR adds tunnels.

TIK marks stable ground.

FINN marks pools.

MARA marks roots.

NINO drops colored fibers at nesting
sites.

AGRA places leaf fragments along ant
routes.

They step back.

The map is beautiful.

PARROT
What do we call it?

DAME DAMSEL
A watershed plan.

PARROT
Too boring.

NINO
The Grand Cooperative Ecological Design.

SPINNER
Too Nino.

BURR
Mud map.

Everyone considers.

DAME DAMSEL
Mud map.

They begin construction.

A rhythmic work sequence develops.

ANTS carry.

BEAVERS place branches.

RODENTS dig.

TERMITES pack earth.

BIRDS carry fibers.

SPIDERS mark lines.

FISH splash at weak points.

FROGS call warnings.

Plants bend.

The stage becomes a machine made of living bodies.

RIVER
Easy.

Easy.

There.

Water enters a newly shaped pool, then continues downstream.

CHEERS.

DAME DAMSEL
Nobody owns that.

BURR
We all built it.

NINO
I did make the flags.

SPINNER
Of course you did.

## SCENE 8 - THE TEMPTATION

EXT. CLEARING - EVENING

PARROT has set up a desk.

A sign reads:

JUNGLE INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY OFFICE
FAST APPROVAL
NO REFUNDS

PARROT
Next!

SKYSHOT approaches.

SKYSHOT
I'd like to patent jumping.

PARROT
Denied.

SKYSHOT
Why?

PARROT
Frogs.

PIP waves.

SKYSHOT
Fine. Jumping from water.

PARROT
Fish.

SKYSHOT
Jumping from water at insects.

PARROT
Still crowded.

SKYSHOT
Can I trademark "SkyShot"?

PARROT
Absolutely.

SKYSHOT
Really?

PARROT
I have no idea.

NINO arrives.

NINO
I want protection for my signature knot.

PARROT
Describe it.

NINO
Nice try.

SPINNER
This office is fake.

PARROT
"Experimental."

AGRA arrives carrying a mushroom.

AGRA
We want to register a shared cultivation
agreement.

PARROT
Shared?

AGRA
Our colony will exchange fungus cultures
with neighboring colonies after floods,
disease, or crop failure.

MARA
And nobody calls fungus property.

AGRA
We're negotiating that sentence.

MARA
We're not.

AGRA
See? Partnership.

NINO looks thoughtful.

NINO
Could I teach weaving and still ask
students to credit who taught them?

JUDGE HORNBILL, entering:

JUDGE HORNBILL
Sounds reasonable.

NINO
Could I refuse to reveal where I hide my
best nesting fibers?

JUDGE HORNBILL
Also reasonable.

NINO
So sharing doesn't mean surrendering
everything?

JUDGE HORNBILL
Who told you it did?

Everyone looks at everyone else.

PARROT
We may have built this entire conflict
on a bad definition.

SPINNER
That would be extremely on-brand for us.

BLACKOUT.

# ACT THREE - THE LIVING COMMONS

## SCENE 9 - SCHOOL

EXT. CLEARING - MORNING

A hand-painted sign:

THE SCHOOL OF THINGS WE KNOW
AND THINGS WE'RE STILL FIGURING OUT

NINO teaches young birds.

NINO
Loop under.

Not over.

Unless the branch bends this way.

Then over.

YOUNG BIRD
Yesterday you said under.

NINO
Yesterday's branch was different.

YOUNG BIRD
So there's no perfect recipe?

NINO
Welcome to nature.

Nearby, SPINNER demonstrates silk.

SPINNER
Copying the shape isn't enough.

You need to respond to the place.

PIP
So the environment is part of the design.

SPINNER
Exactly.

PIP
Can I quote you?

SPINNER
Credit me.

PIP
Deal.

At another station, BURR and TIK compare structures.

BURR
I dig escape routes.

TIK
We build networks.

BURR
I reinforce loose soil.

TIK
We regulate internal conditions.

BURR
Your tunnels are still tiny.

TIK
Your ventilation remains primitive.

They shake paw and antenna.

BURR
Friends?

TIK
Absolutely not.

BURR
Good.

At the water, PROFESSOR FINN speaks to young animals.

PROFESSOR FINN
Different cichlid species solve family
life differently.

Some guard territories. Some guard
offspring. Some carry eggs or young in
their mouths.

SKYSHOT
And some fish leap for bugs.

PROFESSOR FINN
This is my class.

SKYSHOT
Cross-disciplinary learning.

FINN sighs.

SKYSHOT
Want the aerial hunting demonstration?

The students cheer.

SKYSHOT
Finally, academia respects me.

He leaps.

SPLASH.

## SCENE 10 - WHAT THE JUNGLE INVENTED

EXT. GREAT CLEARING - SUNSET

JUDGE HORNBILL convenes the final court.

JUDGE HORNBILL
We began with a question.

Who owns knowledge?

PARROT
I have several answers and a newsletter.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Nobody subscribed.

PARROT
Yet.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Agra?

AGRA
Knowledge can belong to a tradition.

But traditions survive by being practiced,
adapted, and sometimes shared.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Nino?

NINO
Skill deserves credit.

Also, apparently, students.

YOUNG BIRD
We're exhausting.

NINO
Deeply.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Spinner?

SPINNER
No design exists outside its environment.

Change the branch, wind, humidity, prey,
and the web changes.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Dame Damsel?

DAME DAMSEL
Engineering changes other lives.

So building gives you responsibility,
not just bragging rights.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Burr?

BURR
Never dig alone in wet soil.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Philosophically.

BURR
That was philosophical.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Finn?

PROFESSOR FINN
Life is full of solutions.

No species has all of them.

JUDGE HORNBILL
SkyShot?

SKYSHOT
I'm still extremely impressive.

PROFESSOR FINN
We know.

SKYSHOT
And...

(beat)

I hunt because insects live above water,
because plants support insects, because
water supports me.

The trick isn't mine alone.

PROFESSOR FINN
There he is.

SKYSHOT
Don't make it weird.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Mara?

MARA
I have nothing to add.

PARROT
Impossible.

MARA
Look down.

The stage darkens.

Beneath the characters, glowing threads
appear.

Roots.

Fungal networks.

Burrows.

Water channels.

Ant tunnels.

Above them, silk threads catch light.

Bird nests hang between branches.

The ensemble slowly fills the stage.

MARA (CONT'D)
You keep imagining yourselves as separate
inventions.

But life keeps connecting the diagrams.

## SCENE 11 - THE BOUQUET

The ensemble forms a loose circle.

BAOBAB
A leaf falls.

An ENSEMBLE LEAF falls.

MARA
Fungi and microbes break it down.

AGRA
Nutrients return to soil.

BAOBAB
Roots take them.

NINO
Branches grow.

SPINNER
Branches hold webs.

PIP
Webs catch insects.

SKYSHOT
Some insects escape.

PIP
Important detail.

SKYSHOT
They become lunch somewhere else.

PROFESSOR FINN
Fish move nutrients through water.

RIVER
Water moves through land.

DAME DAMSEL
Dams reshape water.

BURR
Burrows reshape soil.

TIK
Soil holds worlds.

MARA
And death feeds life again.

Silence.

JUDGE HORNBILL
So where does one invention end?

No answer.

JUDGE HORNBILL (CONT'D)
Where does one creature end?

MARA
At the skin, perhaps.

BAOBAB
But not at the consequence.

PARROT
I'm writing that down.

JUDGE HORNBILL walks to center.

JUDGE HORNBILL
This court therefore rejects the idea
that the jungle is a warehouse of
separate geniuses guarding separate
treasures.

NINO
Strong wording.

JUDGE HORNBILL
It recognizes craft.

It recognizes effort.

It recognizes traditions, boundaries,
credit, care, and responsibility.

But above all--

He looks around.

JUDGE HORNBILL (CONT'D)
It recognizes dependence.

AGRA takes a small piece of fungus culture
to a neighboring ant.

NINO hands grass fiber to a young bird.

SPINNER stretches a thread between two
branches.

BURR opens a tunnel.

DAME DAMSEL releases water through the
dam.

SKYSHOT leaps.

PIP jumps out of his way.

PIP
Hey!

SKYSHOT
Sorry!

PIP
You absolutely were not!

Laughter.

## SCENE 12 - FINALE

Music emerges from the ecosystem itself.

Water.

Wingbeats.

Frog calls.

Wood tapping.

Leaves.

The rhythm grows.

PARROT
We wanted to know who owned the jungle's
ideas.

AGRA
Turns out the jungle had another question.

NINO
What good is an idea if the world around
it collapses?

SPINNER
What good is a perfect web without
branches?

PROFESSOR FINN
A fish without water?

BURR
A tunnel without soil?

DAME DAMSEL
A dam without a river?

MARA
A fungus without partners?

BAOBAB
A tree without yesterday's dead leaves?

The ensemble closes in.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Every creature changes its environment.

Every environment changes its creatures.

No nest is merely a nest.

No burrow merely a hole.

No dam merely timber.

No web merely silk.

No fungus garden merely food.

They are relationships made visible.

The jungle brightens.

JUDGE HORNBILL (CONT'D)
That is why this place breathes.

Not because everyone is the same.

Not because nobody competes.

Not because every secret must disappear.

It breathes because difference does not
cancel dependence.

The creatures listen.

JUDGE HORNBILL (CONT'D)
Each life brings something.

Each life takes something.

Each life leaves something behind.

Together, they make a living bouquet.

PARROT
Bouquets don't breathe.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Parrot.

PARROT
Sorry.

JUDGE HORNBILL
A living, breathing bouquet.

PARROT
Much better.

JUDGE HORNBILL
And its strongest thread is not ownership.

SPINNER
Careful.

JUDGE HORNBILL
Not even silk.

SPINNER
Acceptable.

JUDGE HORNBILL
It is interdependence.

A long beat.

RIVER
Ready?

DAME DAMSEL
Ready.

RIVER
Then open it.

DAME DAMSEL removes a branch.

Water flows.

Lights ripple through the ensemble.

The creatures return to their activities,
but now those activities overlap.

Ants carry leaves beneath a bird's nest.

A spider anchors silk to a branch.

A frog shelters beneath a leaf.

Fish move through the water.

A beaver repairs the bank.

A rodent digs around roots rather than
through them.

Mushrooms emerge beside the tree.

The jungle becomes a single moving image.

BAOBAB
Nobody lives alone.

MARA
Nobody creates alone.

AGRA
Nobody survives alone.

NINO
But I still want credit for that knot.

SPINNER
Fine.

NINO
Thank you.

PARROT
Breaking news!

Everyone groans.

PARROT (CONT'D)
Jungle survives argument!

JUDGE HORNBILL
That's your headline?

PARROT
Wait.

He thinks.

PARROT (CONT'D)
"Jungle Discovers Everyone Needs
Everyone."

BURR
Bit sentimental.

TIK
Accurate, though.

PARROT
I'll take it.

The ensemble faces the audience.

ALL
Nothing lives alone.

BLACKOUT.

A moment of darkness.

Then the sound of one small insect.

Another answers.

Then a frog.

A bird.

Water.

Wind through leaves.

The sounds overlap until the jungle is
audible again.

FADE OUT.

THE END
